    {
      "id": "",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Rules:",
          "offset": 587
        }
      ],
      "range": {
        "start": 587,
        "end": 593
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "",
      "type": "bulletListItem",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "A ",
          "offset": 597
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "covers",
          "styles": {
            "code": true
          },
          "offset": 600
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " edge means the plan builds the whole rule, so one covering plan discharges it. A rule covered by more than one plan counts as planned only once none of those plans is a draft: until then the rule is ",
          "offset": 607
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "plan-draft",
          "styles": {
            "code": true
          },
          "offset": 808
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ". This is how a rule shared by plans that each build part of it is reported until it is split (WL-SPEC-77 §19).",
          "offset": 819
        }
      ],
      "range": {
        "start": 595,
        "end": 931
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "",
      "type": "bulletListItem",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Only requirements are reported. An invariant or informative rule is never a gap.",
          "offset": 934
        }
      ],
      "range": {
        "start": 932,
        "end": 1014
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "",
      "type": "bulletListItem",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "A deferral discharges nothing. It names who is owed the rest, and the report prints the owner beside the anchor: the owner's slug, or the reference verbatim when it did not resolve. A draft plan's deferral classifies nothing. A deferral is delivered when any plan discharges ",
          "offset": 1017
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "S",
          "styles": {
            "code": true
          },
          "offset": 1293
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "; the owner is never a gate on who may deliver.",
          "offset": 1295
        }
      ],
      "range": {
        "start": 1015,
        "end": 1342
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "",
      "type": "bulletListItem",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "An undischarged section reports the strongest outcome that applies: ",
          "offset": 1345
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "plan-draft",
          "styles": {
            "code": true
          },
          "offset": 1414
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " over ",
          "offset": 1425
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "deferred",
          "styles": {
            "code": true
          },
          "offset": 1432
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " over ",
          "offset": 1441
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "unplanned",
          "styles": {
            "code": true
          },
          "offset": 1448
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ".",
          "offset": 1458
        }
      ],
      "range": {
        "start": 1343,
        "end": 1459
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "",
      "type": "bulletListItem",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "A whole-document ",
          "offset": 1462
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "covers",
          "styles": {
            "code": true
          },
          "offset": 1480
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " entry resolves to every requirement of the document when the plan is written, so it covers each of them.",
          "offset": 1487
        }
      ],
      "range": {
        "start": 1460,
        "end": 1592
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "",
      "type": "bulletListItem",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Overlap is legal: two plans covering one section is two plans touching it.",
          "offset": 1595
        }
      ],
      "range": {
        "start": 1593,
        "end": 1669
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "",
      "type": "bulletListItem",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "A plan whose ",
          "offset": 1672
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "covers",
          "styles": {
            "code": true
          },
          "offset": 1686
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " is ",
          "offset": 1693
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "NO-SPEC",
          "styles": {
            "code": true
          },
          "offset": 1698
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " (§3.3) contributes to nothing and is never itself a gap.",
          "offset": 1706
        }
      ],
      "range": {
        "start": 1670,
        "end": 1764
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "",
      "type": "bulletListItem",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "A deleted document takes part on neither end.",
          "offset": 1767
        }
      ],
      "range": {
        "start": 1765,
        "end": 1812
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "A spec is listed when at least one requirement section is not planned, with the gap count, the anchors, and each anchor's outcome:",
          "offset": 1814
        }
      ],
      "range": {
        "start": 1814,
        "end": 1944
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "",
      "type": "codeBlock",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "WL-SPEC-\u003cn\u003e   accepted   3/9 need planning   sec-2.4(plan-draft) sec-4(unplanned) sec-6(deferred:\u003cowner\u003e)\n",
          "offset": 1950
        }
      ],
      "range": {
        "start": 1946,
        "end": 2059
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Planning coverage and implementation coverage are different questions. ",
          "offset": 2061
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "covers",
          "styles": {
            "code": true
          },
          "offset": 2133
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " says someone undertook to build a section; ",
          "offset": 2140
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "implements",
          "styles": {
            "code": true
          },
          "offset": 2185
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " says the running code satisfies it (WL-SPEC-77 §13).",
          "offset": 2196
        }
      ],
      "range": {
        "start": 2061,
        "end": 2250
      }
    }
  ]
